---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
---
<Layout title="Don't Be Broke — Rahul Jain">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href={base + "origins/"}>&larr; Origins</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Don't Be Broke</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Co-founder, non-profit &middot; Winter 2018</p>
    <section>
      <p class="blurb">
        Don't Be Broke started as a pitch at Seattle Startup Weekend, built on the financial-literacy gap
        I'd identified through the MIT Inspire research: <strong>democratizing financial knowledge for teens</strong> who
        weren't getting it anywhere else. The concept won "Best Design" and "Audience Choice" at the
        event, which was enough momentum to turn it into an actual non-profit developing financial
        literacy materials.
      </p>
      <p class="blurb">
        It was my first time taking an idea all the way from a research question to something with a
        team, a pitch, and real output — a preview of the <strong>"own it end to end"</strong> pattern that shows up in
        everything I've done since.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
